  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 246 PM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nSimilar pleasant conditions will hold through the weekend. A weak \ndisturbance if forecast to sweep across Minnesota; while some model \nguidance hints at light shower activity in northern Iowa, \nprecipitation chances have been kept out of the forecast. Weak \nforcing combined with low to mid level dry air will cause any rain \naloft to evaporate before reaching the ground. Behind this system, a \nreinforced push of dry air will settle into central Iowa, \neliminating any significant rainfall chances for the first full week \nof October. By mid next week, an upper level ridge building over \nthe Four Corners will bring temperatures back into the 70s.",
